notes = "(!) The C64's BASIC, KERNAL and character ROMs go in the system folder (any file names: they are found by their contents).|(!) Disk images need the two 1541 ROMs as well; without them drive 8 is off.|(!) What the drive or the datasette writes is kept in the save folder (name.g64, name.tap); your own image files are never written.|(!) A CMD HD hard drive is the file name.dhd in the save folder (device 12); it needs the CMD HD boot ROM in the system folder. Frontends can make ready drives with the core's kernal64_make_hard_drive (needs the utilities disk too).|(!) Select opens the on-screen keyboard; every RetroPad button can be mapped to a C64 key in the core options."

description = "A cycle-exact Commodore 64 built from the chips' documentation: the 6510, the VIC-II (six models), both CIA generations, the 6581 and 8580 SID with its filter, and a 1541 drive emulated down to its read circuit running its own DOS. Cartridges of many hardware types, disk images (D64, G64 and NIB read directly), tapes, programs; joystick, paddles, the 1351 mouse and a light pen."
